--- !u!114 &5085186621799690852
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 9030685023667656772}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 493a792bf73abbd4bbcca5f2a4ee56ff, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  TargetText: {fileID: 16098351388852271}
  PageCount: {fileID: 3240656791194063088}
  TextArray:
  - "Back before all four megacorps rose to prominence, a <color=#0DBDBF><b>disabled
    bird, <color=#87F8FA>Arkae</color>, glanced up at the sky and yearned to explore
    it</b></color>. He would see his friends, his family, and even his beloved wife
    live his dream... but he remained firmly planted to the ground. \r\n\r\nIt was
    isolating..."
  - 'And yet, when he stared down in despair, what looked back at him were his two
    functioning hands. He realized that, while his wings may be broken, the rest
    of himself was not.


    Trial after trial, <color=#0DBDBF><b>he worked to build</b></color>
    his way into the sky.


    But that obsession only increased his isolation...'
  - 'He was so focused that he didn''t realize when <color=#0DBDBF><b>his wife grew
    sick and passed</b></color>...


    He was so focused that he didn''t realize
    when his children left him...


    And he didn''t even notice when the increase
    in manufacturing <color=#0DBDBF><b>left the skys too polluted</b></color> for
    any winged creature to fly.'
  - 'BUT HIS ISOLATION HAD BEEN WORTH IT!


    After a decade of work, he felt the
    ground leave his talons...


    HE HAD SINGLE HANDEDLY CRAFTED <color=#0DBDBF><b>THE
    FIRST AIRPLANE</b></color>, USING HARD WORK AND DETERMINATION!'
  - 'And yet, when he returned home to boast of his accomplishment... he found the
    ruin his home had been left in... of the life he now had.


    Some say that
    the loss broke him, driving him insane. However, us believers know better. We
    know it gave him both resolve and truth. He was sure that <color=#0DBDBF><b>heaven
    had to be just a little bit higher, and that once he found it, that he could
    see his wife again</b></color>.'
  - He was quick to monitize his invention, forming a monopoly over the pollutant-forbidden
    sky. His business grew quickly, and he invested every last dollar he earned to
    soar even higher! And amongst his new employees, <color=#0DBDBF><b>he promoted
    his four most trusted engineers to be his apprentices</b></color>.
  - 'He and his apprentices toiled around the clock, determined to get up to the
    moon... and then even higher. They sent probe after probe beyond the rays of
    our sun, beyond our galaxy, and even beyond the edges of our universe!


    And
    with that progress, they arrived at what <color=#87F8FA>Arkae</color> called
    his <color=#0DBDBF><b>''final launch''</b></color>. He announced that instead
    of a probe, that he and his apprentices would be manning the next flight. He
    said that they had discovered heaven, and that he had to leave at once.'
  - 'Once he left, years passed without news. Many accused him of being a suicidal
    trillionare...


    But one day, and without warning... <color=#0DBDBF><b>one
    of his apprentices returned, crying tears of joy</b></color>! He announced that
    <color=#87F8FA>Arkae</color> had arrived in heaven, and that he had found it...
    lacking...


    The afterlife was empty, nothing but lost souls, doomed to wander
    an empty void forever.'
  - 'The apprentice announced that <color=#87F8FA>Arkae</color> had completed one
    dream, and founded a new one. Him and three of his apprentices would stay behind,
    to build a true paradise. As for the returned apprentice, he was sent home, to
    recruit more builder''s for <color=#87F8FA>Arkae</color>''s cause!


    <color=#0DBDBF><b>Building
    an afterlife was no trivial task, possibly an infinite one, one that we all had
    to contribute toward!</b></color>'
  - 'As for that apprentice, his name is <color=#87F8FA>Saleos</color>, the wisest
    of those that remain. And as <color=#87F8FA>Arkae</color>''s will dictated, <color=#87F8FA>Saleos</color>,
    as the only remaining apprentice, inherited <color=#87F8FA>Arkae</color>''s fortune,
    business, and purpose.


    <color=#0DBDBF><b>For over three centuries now,
    <color=#87F8FA>Saleos</color> has lived and guided flock.</b></color>'
  StartingIdx: 0
